        "original_id": "18ec0539-8024-5a4a-a01b-0c37795a35fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Xawery Żuławski, Brian G. Hutton, Dorota Masłowska\n- Films: Polish-Russian War, Night Watch, Where Eagles Dare, Kelly's Heroes\n- Places: Warsaw\n- Roles: film directors, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Brian G. Hutton was born on January 1, 1935, and he was an American actor and film director.\n- Xawery Żuławski was born on 22 December 1971 in Warsaw, and he is a Polish film director.\n- Night Watch is a 1973 British suspense-thriller film directed by Brian G. Hutton.\n- Brian G. Hutton's most notable credits include the action films Where Eagles Dare (1968) and Kelly's Heroes (1970).\n- Polish-Russian War is a 2009 Polish film directed by Xawery Żuławski.\n- Polish-Russian War is based on the novel Polish-Russian War under the white-red flag by Dorota Masłowska.\n- Brian G. Hutton died on August 19, 2014.",
